   "rich_text": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": {
      "content": "Rule 1: Store the minimum necessary",
      "link": null
     },
     "annotations": {
      "bold": true,
      "italic": false,
      "strikethrough": false,
      "underline": false,
      "code": false,
      "color": "default"
     },
     "plain_text": "Rule 1: Store the minimum necessary",
     "href": null
    }
   ],
   "is_toggleable": false,
   "color": "default"
  },
  "archived": false
 },
 {
  "object": "block",
  "id": "416004c4-ef7b-40ee-9cd1-45c3be7d3c20",
  "parent": {
   "type": "page_id",
   "page_id": "36694183-19f3-80ce-af6c-fc32055e0f26"
  },
  "created_time": "2026-05-20T09:39:00.000Z",
  "last_edited_time": "2026-05-20T09:39:00.000Z",
  "created_by": {
   "object": "user",
   "id": "231d872b-594c-81f2-a375-0002b8783aca"
  },
  "last_edited_by": {
   "object": "user",
   "id": "231d872b-594c-81f2-a375-0002b8783aca"
  },
  "has_children": false,
  "in_trash": false,
  "type": "paragraph",
  "paragraph": {
   "rich_text": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": {
      "content": "The most common memory mistake is storing too much. Developers configure agents to capture everything a user says on the assumption that more context is always better. It is not.",
      "link": null
     },
     "annotations": {
      "bold": false,
      "italic": false,
      "strikethrough": false,
      "underline": false,
      "code": false,
      "color": "default"
     },
     "plain_text": "The most common memory mistake is storing too much. Developers configure agents to capture everything a user says on the assumption that more context is always better. It is not.",
     "href": null
    }
   ],
   "icon": null,
   "color": "default"
  },
  "archived": false
 },
 {
  "object": "block",
  "id": "83d7ff53-8356-4f63-a940-3446215c845a",
  "parent": {
   "type": "page_id",
   "page_id": "36694183-19f3-80ce-af6c-fc32055e0f26"
  },
  "created_time": "2026-05-20T09:39:00.000Z",
  "last_edited_time": "2026-05-20T09:39:00.000Z",
  "created_by": {
   "object": "user",
   "id": "231d872b-594c-81f2-a375-0002b8783aca"
  },
  "last_edited_by": {
   "object": "user",
   "id": "231d872b-594c-81f2-a375-0002b8783aca"
  },
  "has_children": false,
  "in_trash": false,
  "type": "paragraph",
  "paragraph": {
   "rich_text": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": {
      "content": "Storing unnecessary content has three concrete costs. It increases the size of the context window on every subsequent turn, which raises token costs and degrades attention quality over long conversations. It fills the long-term memory database with noise that makes relevant retrieval harder. And it creates a larger surface area for privacy exposure if the database is ever accessed without authorisation.",
      "link": null
     },
     "annotations": {
      "bold": false,
      "italic": false,
      "strikethrough": false,
      "underline": false,
      "code": false,
      "color": "default"
     },
     "plain_text": "Storing unnecessary content has three concrete costs. It increases the size of the context window on every subsequent turn, which raises token costs and degrades attention quality over long conversations. It fills the long-term memory database with noise that makes relevant retrieval harder. And it creates a larger surface area for privacy exposure if the database is ever accessed without authorisation.",
     "href": null
    }
   ],
   "icon": null,
   "color": "default"
  },
  "archived": false
 },
 {
  "object": "block",
  "id": "2bddd6b2-f91e-4359-bbf3-42cd057a90ed",
  "parent": {
   "type": "page_id",
   "page_id": "36694183-19f3-80ce-af6c-fc32055e0f26"
  },
  "created_time": "2026-05-20T09:39:00.000Z",
  "last_edited_time": "2026-05-20T09:39:00.000Z",
  "created_by": {
   "object": "user",
   "id": "231d872b-594c-81f2-a375-0002b8783aca"
  },
  "last_edited_by": {
   "object": "user",
   "id": "231d872b-594c-81f2-a375-0002b8783aca"
  },
  "has_children": false,
  "in_trash": false,
  "type": "paragraph",
  "paragraph": {
   "rich_text": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": {
      "content": "The rule is simple: store only what the agent would genuinely use in a future interaction to serve the client better. If there is no clear answer to the question \"how would remembering this improve the next conversation?\", the information should not be stored.",
      "link": null
     },
     "annotations": {
      "bold": false,
      "italic": false,
      "strikethrough": false,
      "underline": false,
      "code": false,
      "color": "default"
     },
     "plain_text": "The rule is simple: store only what the agent would genuinely use in a future interaction to serve the client better. If there is no clear answer to the question \"how would remembering this improve the next conversation?\", the information should not be stored.",
     "href": null
    }
   ],
   "icon": null,
   "color": "default"
  },
  "archived": false
 },
 {
